# What `gcloud builds submit --ignore-file=infra/gcp/gcloudignore` uploads. Without it gcloud falls back to the repo's
# ignore rules, and anything not matched there is uploaded to the build bucket. Secrets and local state first, then
# the top-level folders that no image reads (each Dockerfile's own .dockerignore narrows the rest). `/.*/` is every
# top-level dot-directory: the repo's git data, CI files, local tool state and caches.
/.*/
.git
**/.env*
**/.run
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/*-key.json
**/credentials*.json
**/service-account*.json
**/node_modules
**/.next
**/.venv
**/__pycache__
**/.screenshots
**/scratchpad
/apps/site/
/art/
/deploy/
/docs/
/e2e/
/evals/
/scripts/
/tests/
/tools/
/adapters/dev/
